(gen_random_uuid(), 'hmrc-tax-specialist-programme-500-posts-20261025', 'global', 'United Kingdom',
'UK HMRC Tax Specialist Programme 2027: 500 Posts, Closes 26 October',
'यूके एचएमआरसी ट्याक्स स्पेसलिस्ट कार्यक्रम २०२७: ५०० पद, २६ अक्टोबरमा बन्द',
'HMRC''s Tax Specialist Programme 2027 offers 500 permanent posts with a starting salary of £37,682–£46,077 and promotion to Grade 7 on completion — but applications close on 26 October 2026 at 11:55 pm UK time, and no Skilled Worker sponsorship is available.',
'एचएमआरसीको ट्याक्स स्पेसलिस्ट कार्यक्रम २०२७ मा ५०० स्थायी पद छन्, सुरुको तलब £३७,६८२–£४६,०७७ र पूरा गरेपछि ग्रेड ७ मा बढुवा — तर आवेदन २६ अक्टोबर २०२६ राति ११:५५ बजे (यूके समय) बन्द हुन्छ, र स्किल्ड वर्कर स्पोन्सरशिप उपलब्ध छैन।',
$$<p>Applications for HM Revenue and Customs' Tax Specialist Programme 2027 close on 26 October 2026 at 11:55 pm UK time. The programme offers 500 permanent posts at Higher Executive Officer grade, with a starting salary of £37,682 to £46,077 depending on location, and automatic promotion to Grade 7 on successful completion. No previous tax experience is needed, and applicants do not need an accounting qualification or a finance-related degree.</p>
<p>That combination is what makes this round worth attention. Trainees get a permanent contract from the first day, a structured three to four year training route, and a salary that rises to £58,541 nationally or £65,869 in London once the programme is complete. The closing date leaves almost no room for delay. One limit must be stated plainly at the start: HMRC's listing says Skilled Worker sponsorship is not available, so this is a route for people who already have the right to work in the UK, not for applicants from Nepal.</p>
<h2>At a glance</h2>
<table>
<tr><th>Conducting body</th><td>HM Revenue and Customs (HMRC), UK</td></tr>
<tr><th>Programme</th><td>Tax Specialist Programme 2027 (reference 484623)</td></tr>
<tr><th>Posts</th><td>500, permanent, full-time or part-time</td></tr>
<tr><th>Starting grade</th><td>Higher Executive Officer</td></tr>
<tr><th>Starting salary</th><td>£37,682–£46,077 (national £37,682–£40,705; London £42,631–£46,077)</td></tr>
<tr><th>Salary after completion</th><td>£58,541 nationally or £65,869 in London, at Grade 7</td></tr>
<tr><th>Programme length</th><td>Approximately 3–4 years (longer for part-time trainees)</td></tr>
<tr><th>Locations</th><td>Belfast, Birmingham, Bristol, Cardiff, Croydon, Edinburgh, Glasgow, Leeds, Liverpool, Manchester, Newcastle-upon-Tyne, Nottingham, Portsmouth, Stratford</td></tr>
<tr><th>Working pattern</th><td>Minimum 28 hours per week; at least 60% office-based</td></tr>
<tr><th>Closing date</th><td>26 October 2026 at 11:55 pm UK time</td></tr>
<tr><th>Skilled Worker sponsorship</th><td>Not available</td></tr>
<tr><th>Official portal</th><td><a href="https://careers.hmrc.gov.uk/jobs/tax-specialist-programme-2027-belfast-united-kingdom-birmingham-bristol-cardiff-croydon-edinburgh-glasgow-leeds-liverpool-manchester-newcastle-upon-tyne-nottingham-portsmouth-stratford">careers.hmrc.gov.uk</a></td></tr>
</table>
<h2>Why it matters</h2>
<p>HMRC is the department that collects the tax revenue funding public services across the UK, from healthcare and education to infrastructure. Its compliance workforce checks that individuals and businesses pay the correct amount, and the Tax Specialist Programme is the department's own structured route for building that workforce. Trainees do not sit on the sidelines: from the start they work on real tax cases involving individuals, businesses and professional advisers, with support from experienced tax professionals, learning specialists and business learning managers.</p>
<p>The permanent contract matters more than it sounds. Many graduate routes start on fixed-term or training-only terms; this one is permanent from day one, and promotion to Grade 7 follows automatically once a trainee meets the programme requirements, rather than through a fresh competition. The benefits package adds weight: a Civil Service pension with an employer contribution of 28.97%, annual leave starting at 25 days and rising to 30 with service, and flexible and hybrid working where business needs allow.</p>
<h2>Key details</h2>
<p>HMRC says it welcomes applications from a wide range of educational and professional backgrounds. The academic bar is a minimum 2:2 degree or equivalent, in any subject. What the programme looks for instead is the ability to work with complex information and competing viewpoints, curiosity and willingness to learn, strong communication and interpersonal skills, professionalism and sound judgement, organisation and time management, resilience, and commitment to a structured professional development programme. Previous tax experience is explicitly not required.</p>
<p>Trainees build specialist knowledge across Corporation Tax, Personal Tax, VAT, Employment Duties and Customs. Day to day, the work includes managing a caseload, investigating tax cases, gathering and evaluating evidence, resolving enquiries, communicating with customers and their representatives by meeting, phone, video call and letter, and applying statutory interest and penalties where appropriate. Alongside the casework, trainees attend classroom-based learning events and programme activities, and travel is required where business needs demand it, including visits away from the home office.</p>
<p>Applicants must select one preferred location when they apply, and HMRC says that preference stays with the candidate throughout the recruitment process. The practical advice is to choose a location the candidate can genuinely travel to and work from if appointed, because the choice cannot be swapped later. Part-time working is possible, with a minimum of 28 hours per week, but HMRC notes that part-time working may extend the overall duration of the programme.</p>
<p>Selection runs in stages. After the online application comes a situational judgement test, followed by numerical and verbal reasoning tests, then a video interview and an assessment centre. Candidates who have prepared for Civil Service style online tests will recognise the shape of the process; candidates who have not should practise the test formats before the closing date, because the tests follow quickly once the window shuts.</p>
<h2>How to apply</h2>
<p>First, settle the location choice before opening the form, since it stays fixed through the process. Second, apply through the official HMRC careers portal before 11:55 pm UK time on 26 October 2026, and do not leave it to the final hours: large closing-date surges slow portals down, and a missed deadline has no appeal. Third, keep the email account used for the application monitored after submission, because test invitations and interview details arrive by email. Fourth, gather degree evidence in advance so the form can be completed in one sitting.</p>
<p>For readers preparing now, the useful order is: confirm eligibility (a 2:2 degree or equivalent, right to work in the UK), pick the location, submit the application, then practise situational judgement, numerical and verbal reasoning tests while waiting for the next stage. The programme starts successful candidates on real responsibility immediately, so evidence of analytical work, resilience and sound judgement from any background — not only tax or finance — is what the assessors are looking for.</p>
<h2>Background</h2>
<p>HMRC describes the programme as its route for developing the next generation of tax professionals within its Compliance Operations Directorate. The structure — practical workplace experience combined with formal learning, independent study and assessments — is designed so that trainees finish as Senior Tax Specialists at Grade 7, able to handle the most complex cases. That is why the programme runs for three to four years rather than a few months: the qualification is the career itself, not a certificate on top of one.</p>
<p>For readers in Nepal, the honest position is that this recruitment is not an application route. HMRC does not offer Skilled Worker sponsorship for these posts, and the programme requires UK office-based working. The caution that applies to every foreign government drive covered here applies again: anyone in Nepal who is offered a seat on this programme for a fee is being scammed. HMRC recruits only through its own careers portal, and it does not charge applicants anything.</p>
<p>The window shuts on 26 October 2026. For eligible UK-based readers, that leaves one clear action: apply through the official portal before 11:55 pm UK time, with the location choice settled and degree evidence ready.</p>$$,
$$<p>यूकेको एचएमआरसी (राजस्व तथा भन्सार विभाग) को ट्याक्स स्पेसलिस्ट कार्यक्रम २०२७ का लागि आवेदन २६ अक्टोबर २०२६ राति ११:५५ बजे (यूके समय) बन्द हुँदैछ। यस कार्यक्रममा ५०० स्थायी पद छन्, सुरुको श्रेणी हायर एक्जिक्युटिभ अफिसर हो, तलब स्थानअनुसार £३७,६८२ देखि £४६,०७७ सम्म छ, र कार्यक्रम सफलतापूर्वक पूरा गरेपछि ग्रेड ७ मा स्वतः बढुवा हुन्छ। यसका लागि पहिले करसम्बन्धी अनुभव, लेखा योग्यता वा वित्तसम्बन्धी डिग्री चाहिँदैन।</p>
<p>यो संयोजन नै यस भर्नाको खास कुरा हो। प्रशिक्षार्थीले पहिलो दिनदेखि स्थायी करार पाउँछन्, तीनदेखि चार वर्षको संरचित तालिम पाउँछन्, र पूरा गरेपछि तलब राष्ट्रिय स्तरमा £५८,५४१ र लन्डनमा £६५,८६९ पुग्छ। तर एउटा सीमा सुरुमै स्पष्ट पार्नुपर्छ: एचएमआरसीको सूचनामा स्किल्ड वर्कर स्पोन्सरशिप उपलब्ध नभएको लेखिएको छ, त्यसैले यो यूकेमा काम गर्ने अधिकार भएकाहरूका लागि मात्र हो, नेपालबाट आवेदन गर्ने बाटो होइन।</p>
