'उत्तर प्रदेश शिक्षा सेवा चयन आयोगले विज्ञापन ०७/२०२६ अन्तर्गत सहायता प्राप्त माध्यमिक विद्यालयहरूमा १७,७३५ सहायक शिक्षक (टीजीटी) पद खोलेको छ — आवेदन २४ अक्टोबरदेखि २३ नोभेम्बर २०२६ सम्म, लिखित परीक्षा २३ र २४ डिसेम्बरमा।',
$$<p>The Uttar Pradesh Education Service Selection Commission (UPESSC) opened applications on 24 October 2026 for 17,735 Assistant Teacher posts at Trained Graduate Teacher (TGT) level, under advertisement number 07/2026. The window closes on 23 November 2026, the correction window stays open until 26 November, and the written examination is scheduled for 23 and 24 December 2026. The posts are in non-government aided secondary schools across Uttar Pradesh, for Classes 6 to 10.</p>
<p>The scale is what stands out. At 17,735 posts, this is one of the largest teacher recruitments Uttar Pradesh has run in a single advertisement: 16,193 posts in boys' schools and 1,542 in girls' schools. The commission has also said the number of vacancies may increase or decrease, so the advertised figure is the working total, not a promise. One honest limit for readers: the notification invites eligible Indian citizens, and the posts are in aided schools rather than directly run government schools — a distinction that matters for service conditions, even though the pay scale is a government one.</p>
<h2>At a glance</h2>
<table>
<tr><th>Conducting body</th><td>Uttar Pradesh Education Service Selection Commission (UPESSC), Prayagraj</td></tr>
<tr><th>Advertisement</th><td>07/2026</td></tr>
<tr><th>Posts</th><td>17,735 Assistant Teacher (TGT) posts — 16,193 in boys' schools, 1,542 in girls' schools</td></tr>
<tr><th>Schools</th><td>Non-government aided secondary schools, Uttar Pradesh, Classes 6 to 10</td></tr>
<tr><th>Pay scale</th><td>Pay Level 7: Rs 44,900–1,42,400, grade pay Rs 4,600</td></tr>
<tr><th>Application window</th><td>24 October to 23 November 2026</td></tr>
<tr><th>Correction window</th><td>Until 26 November 2026</td></tr>
<tr><th>Written examination</th><td>23 and 24 December 2026</td></tr>
<tr><th>Application fee</th><td>General / OBC / EWS Rs 1,000; SC / ST Rs 500; PH Rs 300</td></tr>
<tr><th>Age limit</th><td>21 to 62 years as on 1 July 2026, with relaxation as per rules</td></tr>
<tr><th>Qualification</th><td>Bachelor's degree in the relevant subject plus B.Ed., and the TET qualification prescribed for the post</td></tr>
<tr><th>Selection</th><td>Written examination (120 questions, 360 marks, 2 hours, 1 mark deducted per wrong answer), then document verification</td></tr>
<tr><th>Official portal</th><td><a href="https://upessc.up.gov.in">upessc.up.gov.in</a></td></tr>
</table>
<h2>Why it matters</h2>
<p>TGT teachers are the backbone of secondary schooling: they teach Classes 6 to 10, the years where students move from general learning to subject streams that decide their later options. A shortage at this level shows up quickly in board results and dropout rates, which is why a single drive of this size matters for the whole state system. The subject spread also tells a story. According to the published vacancy details, Hindi carries the highest count at 2,791 posts, followed by English at 2,517, Science at 2,493, Social Science at 2,482 and Mathematics at 2,349, with Sanskrit, Urdu, Commerce, Music, Home Science, Physical Education, Art, Agriculture and other subjects making up the rest.</p>
<p>For candidates, the Pay Level 7 scale is the practical draw: a starting basic of Rs 44,900 with the allowances that come with a government pay scale, in a post that carries the security of aided-school service. The age window is unusually wide — 21 to 62 years as on 1 July 2026 — which keeps the drive open to experienced teachers as well as fresh B.Ed. graduates, though candidates must confirm the relaxation rules and subject-wise conditions in the detailed notification before applying.</p>
<h2>Key details</h2>
<p>The application process has one step candidates must not skip: One-Time Registration (OTR) on the UPESSC portal, which must be completed before the main form can be filled. Applicants should check that personal details, educational qualifications and category information are accurate at the OTR stage, because errors there follow the application through verification. The written examination carries 120 multiple-choice questions for 360 marks in two hours, with one mark deducted for each wrong answer — a pattern that rewards accuracy over guessing, and one that candidates should build into their practice.</p>
<p>Eligibility turns on three things: a bachelor's degree in the relevant subject, a B.Ed. qualification, and the TET qualification the notification prescribes for the post. Subject-wise requirements differ, and candidates should read the detailed advertisement for their subject rather than assuming a general rule covers them. The commission has kept the fee structure simple — Rs 1,000 for General, OBC and EWS candidates, Rs 500 for SC and ST candidates, and Rs 300 for physically handicapped candidates — payable online through the portal.</p>
<h2>How to apply</h2>
<p>First, complete One-Time Registration on upessc.up.gov.in and verify every detail in it. Second, fill the main application form for the correct subject and school category, and pay the fee before 23 November 2026 — the fee and the form share the same last date, so a form without a paid fee is not a complete application. Third, use the correction window until 26 November 2026 to fix any error, and keep a printed copy of the final submitted form. Fourth, prepare documents now for the verification stage: degree certificates, B.Ed. certificate, TET qualification, category certificate where applicable, and identity proof.</p>
<p>For examination preparation, the useful order is: the prescribed syllabus for the subject, previous years' TGT papers for the 120-question pattern, and timed practice with negative marking in mind. Candidates who treat the two-hour paper as a speed test and guess freely will lose marks to the deduction rule; candidates who answer what they know and leave what they do not will protect their score.</p>
<h2>Background</h2>
<p>UPESSC, based in Prayagraj, is the commission that recruits teachers for Uttar Pradesh's aided secondary schools, and TGT recruitment is its most-watched exercise because it feeds the classrooms where the state's secondary results are made. Aided schools sit between fully government schools and private ones: they are privately managed but government-aided, which is why their teachers are recruited through a public commission and paid on a government scale. That structure is also why the detailed notification, rather than any summary, is the final word on subject-wise vacancies, qualifications and service conditions.</p>
<p>For readers in Nepal, the same caution as with every Indian state drive applies: this recruitment is for eligible Indian citizens, and no agent can secure a seat in it. Anyone in Nepal who is asked to pay for a place in this drive is being targeted by a scam. The legitimate route is the UPESSC portal alone, and it charges only the published examination fee.</p>
<p>The window closes on 23 November 2026, with the examination on 23 and 24 December. For eligible candidates, the practical sequence is OTR first, form and fee before 23 November, correction before 26 November, and examination preparation built around the 120-question, negative-marking pattern.</p>$$,
$$<p>उत्तर प्रदेश शिक्षा सेवा चयन आयोग (यूपीएसएससी) ले २४ अक्टोबर २०२६ देखि प्रशिक्षित स्नातक शिक्षक (टीजीटी) तहका १७,७३५ सहायक शिक्षक पदका लागि आवेदन खोलेको छ, विज्ञापन नम्बर ०७/२०२६ अन्तर्गत। आवेदनको म्याद २३ नोभेम्बर २०२६ मा सकिन्छ, सच्याउने म्याद २६ नोभेम्बरसम्म खुला रहन्छ, र लिखित परीक्षा २३ र २४ डिसेम्बर २०२६ मा हुनेछ। यी पद उत्तर प्रदेशका सहायता प्राप्त माध्यमिक विद्यालयहरूमा कक्षा ६ देखि १० सम्मका लागि हुन्।</p>
<p>यसको आकार नै खास कुरा हो। एउटै विज्ञापनमा १७,७३५ पद — केटाहरूका विद्यालयमा १६,१९३ र केटीहरूका विद्यालयमा १,५४२ — उत्तर प्रदेशले एकैपटक चलाएको सबैभन्दा ठूलो शिक्षक भर्नामध्ये एक हो। आयोगले पद संख्या बढ्न वा घट्न सक्ने पनि बताएको छ, त्यसैले विज्ञापित संख्या कामचलाउ कुल हो, वाचा होइन। एउटा इमानदार सीमा: सूचनाले योग्य भारतीय नागरिकलाई आमन्त्रण गरेको छ, र यी पद प्रत्यक्ष सरकारी विद्यालयका होइन, सहायता प्राप्त विद्यालयका हुन् — तलब सरकारी मापदण्डकै भए पनि सेवा सर्तमा फरक पर्छ।</p>
<h2>एक झलक</h2>
