<tr><th>Advertisement</th><td>01/2026</td></tr>
<tr><th>Posts</th><td>815 regular posts — Principal, PGT, TGT, Art Teacher, Physical Education Teacher, Computer Teacher</td></tr>
<tr><th>Schools</th><td>Odisha Adarsha Vidyalayas (OAVs) and Odisha Mining Adarsha Vidyalayas (OMAVs)</td></tr>
<tr><th>Application window</th><td>12 October to 11 November 2026, 5:00 pm</td></tr>
<tr><th>Mode</th><td>Online only, through oav.edu.in</td></tr>
<tr><th>Pay levels (ORSP Rules, 2017)</th><td>Principal Level 13 (about Rs 67,700 per month); PGT Level 11 (about Rs 47,600); TGT and Art Teacher Level 10 (about Rs 44,900); PET and Computer Teacher Level 9 (about Rs 35,400)</td></tr>
<tr><th>Age limit (as on 1 January 2026)</th><td>Principal 32 to 50 years; teachers 21 to 42 years, with relaxation as per Odisha government rules</td></tr>
<tr><th>Application fee</th><td>Principal: UR and SEBC Rs 2,000, SC, ST and PwD Rs 1,250; Teachers: UR and SEBC Rs 1,500, SC, ST and PwD Rs 1,000</td></tr>
<tr><th>Selection</th><td>Computer Based Test, then interview or performance test where applicable</td></tr>
<tr><th>Official portal</th><td><a href="https://oav.edu.in">oav.edu.in</a></td></tr>
</table>
<h2>Why it matters</h2>
<p>Adarsha Vidyalayas are Odisha's model schools, set up to give students in every block access to quality secondary education without leaving their district. The OMAV network extends the same model to mining-affected areas. A recruitment of 815 regular posts into that system is therefore not a routine vacancy round: it decides who leads and teaches in schools that anchor their local education map. Regular status is the key word. Contract teachers live with renewal uncertainty; regular appointees carry the service protections, increments and retirement framework of state government service.</p>
<p>The Principal posts deserve separate attention. With over 100 headships on offer, this drive is also a leadership pipeline: experienced teachers and administrators who meet the Principal conditions can move into running a school, rather than waiting for a seniority-based promotion inside one institution. For PGT and TGT candidates, the draw is the same as in other state teacher drives — a government pay level, a defined career path, and postings across the state's school network rather than a single district.</p>
<h2>Key details</h2>
<p>Qualifications differ sharply by post, and candidates should match themselves to the right one before applying. Principal posts ask for a master's degree with at least 45% aggregate marks, a B.Ed. from an NCTE-recognised institution, and relevant administrative or teaching experience. PGT posts ask for a master's degree in the relevant subject with at least 50% marks (45% for SC, ST, SEBC and PwD candidates) plus a B.Ed. TGT posts ask for a bachelor's degree in the relevant subject with at least 50% marks (45% for reserved categories), a B.Ed., and an OSSTET, OTET Paper-II or CTET Paper-II qualification. Computer Teacher posts accept a B.E. or B.Tech. in Computer Science or IT, MCA, M.Sc. in IT or Computer Science, BCA, B.Sc. in Computer Science, or a DOEACC or NIELIT 'B' level qualification. Art posts ask for a bachelor's degree in Fine Arts or Visual Arts, and PET posts ask for a B.P.Ed. or M.P.Ed. Teachers are also expected to be able to teach in both English and Odia medium.</p>
<p>Age limits are set as on 1 January 2026: above 32 and below 50 years for Principal posts, and above 21 and below 42 years for other posts, with standard relaxations for SC, ST, SEBC, women, PwD and ex-servicemen candidates as per Odisha government rules. The fee structure is two-tiered: Principal applicants pay Rs 2,000 (UR and SEBC) or Rs 1,250 (SC, ST and PwD), while teacher applicants pay Rs 1,500 (UR and SEBC) or Rs 1,000 (SC, ST and PwD), payable online.</p>
<p>Selection runs through a Computer Based Test of multiple-choice questions, followed by an interview or a practical performance test where applicable for shortlisted candidates. Candidates should therefore prepare in two parts: subject and general content for the CBT, and classroom or leadership demonstration for the later stage, since a strong CBT score alone does not close the process.</p>
<h2>How to apply</h2>
<p>First, register on oav.edu.in with a valid email address and mobile number, since login credentials arrive through them. Second, fill the form with post preferences that match the qualifications held — a PGT application with a bachelor's degree alone, or a Principal application without the required experience, will fail verification no matter how well the CBT goes. Third, upload the photograph, signature and certificates in the required format, and pay the fee for the correct category before submitting. Fourth, keep a printed copy of the final submitted form, and apply well before 5:00 pm on 11 November 2026, when the portal closes and last-hour traffic peaks.</p>
<p>For preparation, the useful order is: the prescribed syllabus for the post, previous OAVS and state teacher CBT papers for the question pattern, and practice in the performance or interview format for the second stage. Principal candidates should additionally prepare evidence of administrative experience and a clear view of how they would run a model school, because the interview stage tests leadership judgement, not only subject knowledge.</p>
<h2>Background</h2>
<p>The Adarsha Vidyalaya system was built to take quality secondary schooling to every block of Odisha, and its staffing has always been a state-level exercise rather than a district one — which is why a single advertisement can carry 815 posts across teaching and leadership. The OMAV schools apply the same model in mining areas, where the state has a direct interest in schooling quality for affected communities. Regular recruitment into this system, as opposed to contractual hiring, is how the state keeps experienced teachers in these schools instead of losing them to the next short-term engagement.</p>
<p>For readers in Nepal, the caution is the same as for every Indian state drive: this recruitment is run by the Odisha state government for its own schools, and no agent can secure a place in it. Anyone in Nepal who is asked to pay for an OAVS seat is being targeted by a scam. The legitimate route is the OAVS portal alone, and it charges only the published application fee.</p>
<p>The window closes on 11 November 2026 at 5:00 pm. For eligible candidates, the practical sequence is registration on oav.edu.in, a post choice that matches the qualifications held, fee payment in the correct category, and preparation split between the CBT and the interview or performance stage.</p>$$,
$$<p>ओडिशा आदर्श विद्यालय संगठन (ओएभीएस) ले १२ अक्टोबर २०२६ देखि ओडिशा आदर्श विद्यालय (ओएभी) र ओडिशा माइनिङ आदर्श विद्यालय (ओएमएभी) मा ८१५ प्रधानाध्यापक र शिक्षक पदका लागि आवेदन खोलेको छ, विज्ञापन नम्बर ०१/२०२६ अन्तर्गत। आवेदनको म्याद ११ नोभेम्बर २०२६ साँझ ५ बजे सकिन्छ। यी पद नियमित नियुक्ति हुन्, करार होइन — जसको अर्थ जागिरको सुरक्षा, सेवा सर्त र निवृत्तिभरण सुविधामा वास्तविक फरक पर्छ।</p>
<p>यो भर्नाले विद्यालय प्रणालीको पूरै तह समेट्छ: १०० भन्दा बढी प्रधानाध्यापक पद, छ विषयमा स्नातकोत्तर शिक्षक (पीजीटी), सबैभन्दा ठूलो समूहका रूपमा प्रशिक्षित स्नातक शिक्षक (टीजीटी), साथै कला शिक्षक, शारीरिक शिक्षा शिक्षक (पीईटी) र कम्प्युटर शिक्षक। एउटै आवेदन अवधिले कक्षा कोठाका पद र विद्यालय नेतृत्वका पद दुवै दिन्छ, तर योग्यता र उमेर सीमा फरक छन्। संख्या बारे एउटा इमानदार सीमा: कुल ८१५ सबै प्रकाशित रिपोर्टमा एउटै छ, तर विषयगत विभाजन माध्यमिक रिपोर्टहरूमा फरक छ, त्यसैले विस्तृत सूचना (oav.edu.in) नै विभाजनको आधिकारिक स्रोत हो, र यस लेखले त्यससँग बाझिने विभाजन जानाजानी प्रकाशित गरेको छैन।</p>
